      "content": "i get that it looks bad now, but some historians argue that the Norwegian government actually fled and left a vacuum. if he didnt step up and try to provide some kind of domestic structure, wouldn't the Germans have just ruled with an even more direct, military-only approach without any local involvement at all? like, was there any benefit to having a local figurehead even if he was working with them?",
